e season that you might want  to pick up if you're looking for  something to kill time and unwind two  [Music]  when i saw the promo art for aqua top  and white sand several titles crossed my  mind there's just a feel to it that any  veteran fan would immediately recognize  and having pa works at the helm further  pushes that impression however what i  didn't expect is for aqua top and white  sand to be as straightforward as it was  now that's not a bad thing necessarily  i'm always up for a slice of life and  the story of a former idol reigniting  her passion for the joys of life is  something that i did have a good time  watching helping with the enjoyment is  seeing pa works pull out their a game  with how they made the backgrounds and  the overall atmosphere so vibrant and  alive the arts definitely the strongest  part of the show and it blows almost  every other element out of the water  people have called this a successor to a  lull in the sea or blossoms for tomorrow  and i can clearly see the similarities  if you're a fan of the aforementioned  series you should give this one a try  it's not nearly as dramatic as the  flagship key titles that people might  associate with the studio but it's still  as heartwarming in its own right  [Music]  coming in at number six is words bubble  up like soda pop and now we have a  surprise movie on the list bet you  didn't see this one coming now did you  for a whole lot of you the boy meets  girl's story of cherry and smile maybe  something that's quite familiar to you  two people coming together falling in  love while becoming each other's pillars  of support as they grow together it's  not the rarest anime movie out there but  this one still hits home when it matters  in letting its charm shine in making you  feel good the story develops like  various other movies of the genre but  the production and the chemistry between  the characters really get a chance to  take the forefront here while somewhat  formulaic the story 