 the old guard to train the new  misfits in the looming battle against  the resurrected demons it's pretty much  supernatural shonen given a very  colourful and wacky visual style thanks  to the two creators involved and of  course some raunchy content but what did  you expect it's pretty surprising to see  mapa work on a show with this visual  style after seeing a common thread among  their big hits but they've done a good  job with this all things considered i  find the show quirky and fun to watch  and if you look closely enough there's  been some clever world building amidst  the fighting and the fan service it  might not be the show now for everyone  but it's something that i'd recommend to  seasoned anime watches  honestly i didn't know what to make of  sony boy before the season started all  in all sony boy indeed is a visual  spectacle with a lot of thought and  meaning put into it i called sony boy an  artsy show and i think that by this  point you can tell the reputation of  something like that you know a show that  is dialogue driven filled with some  insights and thoughts about humanity to  go with its drama along with visuals  that can probably put any non-theatrical  productions to shame it also eschews  most of the high octane action that  often comes associated with the premise  of being lost in a dimension with  superpowers it takes things slowly and  methodically yes sony boy is a slow show  and it requires a lot of attention and  thought on the part of the viewer that's  to say that it's not a show for everyone  but it does have its niche and if you  happen to fall into said niche i think  that this show can be a strong contender  for anime of the season  ugh  talk about a surprise entry it aired  quite late into the season but fenner  pirate princess is quickly becoming the  rising star of the summer 2021 season  surpassing all expectations as i can see  i know the fact that i promoted it on  this channel a few videos back is not a  reason for me placing it as number two  on the list the show's legitimately good  in a lot of ways and it pretty much blew  away all expectations i had when i  started covering it at first glance it  seems to be a typical adventure  featuring a plucky girl on a quest for  treasure i mean i felt that way too  until i actually watched the show and  got enthralled by the adventure of  self-discovery it really does give some  yonah of the dawn vibes and i'm sure  that a lot of people have pointed that  out but to a lesser extent i can see  some of snow white with red hair and i  really enjoyed that show as well what i  like about fenner is that i can  immediately tell that the show's been  given the love and care that it deserves  during production that much can be  reflected in the visuals the detailing  and the background music for an anime  original by production ig this is  looking very promising even though it  hasn't had as many episodes as most of  its seasonal peers if you're out for an  adventure story with some themes of  family and self-discovery then our  pirate princess is definitely worth the  watch  foreign  [Music]  and here my friends at the top of the  list is a show that definitely didn't  disappoint in my preseason video i  praised the show to high heavens for its  unique visual appeal it's enchanting  music buys for yuki kajura aside and its  execution of the whole victorian europe  setting consider those expectations met  and i can confidently say that the case  study of vanitas is a legit contender  for anime of the season whether i take  into account my personal opinions or not  what starts off as a premise of a  mystery slowly unravels into a very  multi-layered story about some striking  themes chief among those the idea of  self-worth and guilt it helps that the  characters come with their own  complexities and intricacies even  characters portrayed to be eccentric  naive or goofy eventually reveal hidden  depths and those work so well with the  story that the narrative is trying to  tell us the complexity along with a  blend of serious and comedic elements  come together to create a show that can  be enjoyed by viewers of all tastes and  interests plus it's got a lot of good  looking guys for the girls while some  scenes have been cut from the manga as  usual i don't think that they really  detract from the experience here in  contrast to the detective is already  dead which i mentioned a while ago i  think the vanitas anime still manages to  capture the magic of the manga in its  own way and that's why i have this as my  number one new anime of summer 2021 all  right  [Music]  how's your list looking then comment  below and let me know i'd love to have a  chat with you about it if you enjoyed  the video don't hesitate to like the  video and subscribe to the channel so  that you can be notified the next time i  upload another video you may also  support the channel via patreon or  memberships and each contribution will  go a long way in allowing me to make  even better videos or giving you a  glimpse of my video making process  that's it for today i hope you had fun  watching and i'll see you next time  [Music]  you

